{"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Encoding-batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchEncoder","doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatch"],"title":"Encoding batches"},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorEncodingError"],"title":"Records left out"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/collectorencoding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" for a self-hosted TraffluentCollector’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/v1\/batches"},{"type":"text","text":". Give it to an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") as its encoder,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and pass the collector’s API key to the destination as an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Authorization: Bearer"},{"type":"text","text":" header field."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The body is JSON: one object per record, with the record’s identifier (which a redelivered record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps), the event’s name, its timestamp, whether it is redelivered, its properties and its context."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read from the event’s "},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" form, which "},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" derives, through the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event’s schema in the "},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with. The context holds the standard"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context keys the record has values for, its session and sample rate, and its trace context. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value is written only while the record reveals it; once redacted, a "},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property is left out, and an array’s element, or a value inside a type the plan can’t map, is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one whose event and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"version the plan doesn’t describe, one whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and one holding a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"JSON can’t, such as a NaN. ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true},{"text":" returns each record left out","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","isActive":true},{"text":"), which the destination logs and reports on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its ","type":"text"},{"code":"dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". When no record of a batch can be written, the destination sends nothing.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchEncoder\/batch(of:)","isActive":true},{"text":" returns the same body and skipped records without a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To send to a server of your own format, write a "},{"code":"BatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" of your own. To send to PostHog,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"use "},{"code":"PostHogBatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"code":"PostHogEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import CollectorEncoding","import HTTPDestinations","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan(schemas: [SignedUp.schema])","let encoder = CollectorBatchEncoder(plan: plan)","let collector = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: collectorURL,  \/\/ https:\/\/collector.example.com\/v1\/batches","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(apiKey)\"],","    encoder: encoder)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: collector)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers sending to the collector beside the other destinations.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Write batches of records in TraffluentCollector’s ingest format, for an "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","t